## Prerequisites
- Node 20+ or Python 3.10+
- An OpenAI API key with Realtime API access
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` set in your environment
- Optional: install the OpenAI Node or Python SDK (v4.x+)

## Install the SDK

```bash
# Node
npm install openai

# Python
pip install openai
```

## Minimal GPT-Realtime-2 session (Node / WebSocket)

```typescript
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI();

// Create a Realtime session
const session = await client.beta.realtime.sessions.create({
  model: "gpt-realtime-2",
  voice: "alloy",
  modalities: ["audio", "text"],
  instructions: "You are a helpful voice assistant.",
  // Reasoning effort: "minimal" | "low" | "medium" | "high" | "xhigh"
  // Default is "low" — good for most conversational use cases
});

console.log("Session ID:", session.id);
console.log("Client secret:", session.client_secret.value);
// Use client_secret.value with WebRTC or WebSocket transport
```

## Connect via WebSocket and send audio

```typescript
import WebSocket from "ws";

const ws = new WebSocket(
  "wss://api.openai.com/v1/realtime?model=gpt-realtime-2",
  {
    headers: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY}`,
      "OpenAI-Beta": "realtime=v1",
    },
  }
);

ws.on("open", () => {
  // Configure the session
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({
    type: "session.update",
    session: {
      modalities: ["audio", "text"],
      voice: "alloy",
      // Add tools here if your agent needs to call APIs
      tools: [],
    },
  }));
});

ws.on("message", (data) => {
  const event = JSON.parse(data.toString());
  if (event.type === "response.audio.delta") {
    // Stream audio bytes to your output device
    const audioChunk = Buffer.from(event.delta, "base64");
    // write to speaker / stream to client
  }
});
```

## Live translation (GPT-Realtime-Translate)

```typescript
const session = await client.beta.realtime.sessions.create({
  model: "gpt-realtime-translate",
  // Input: spoken language detected automatically from 70+ supported
  // Output: one of the 13 supported output languages
  output_language: "en",
});
```

## Streaming transcription only (GPT-Realtime-Whisper)

```typescript
const session = await client.beta.realtime.sessions.create({
  model: "gpt-realtime-whisper",
  modalities: ["text"],  // text only — returns transcripts, no audio output
});
// Billed at $0.017 / minute
```

## Gotcha: reasoning effort vs. latency
Leaving reasoning at `xhigh` makes GPT-Realtime-2 pause noticeably before answering simple questions. Use `low` (default) for conversational turns and only escalate to `high`/`xhigh` when the task requires multi-step reasoning (e.g. complex tool orchestration).

